{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789243180,"nonce":"C11q1O4pW6Wslf4/Vq8RupYJZ/g=","title":"binarytrees 7x slower: unannotated constructor parameters lost the type of the field they feed","message":"CI Benchmarks, kernel binarytrees, every rayzor target: ~360 ms at 647a7f0b,\n~3100 ms from 42ee91e2 on (llvm 362 -\u003e 2593, cranelift 391 -\u003e 2628,\nprecompiled 393 -\u003e 1806, tiered 375 -\u003e 2830). The other four kernels are\nunchanged. Locally `rayzor run --llvm --release` on\ncompiler/benchmarks/src/binarytrees.hx went 1.4 s -\u003e 0.45 s wall with the fix.\n\nMechanism (585b2709): `infer_unannotated_param_types` runs once per class\nbefore any member is lowered, so the signatures and the bodies agree. It\nseeds from `param_types_from_field_stores`, which looks the stored-into\nfield up in `class_fields` — but only METHODS are pre-registered at that\npoint; the class's own `var` fields are registered when they are lowered,\nin the member loop that ran after. So for `new(left, right, item)\n{ this.left = left; ... }` the recovery found no field, recorded an EMPTY\nmap for the constructor, and the body-time fallback (which used to run\nafter the fields existed) was skipped because an entry was present. All\nthree parameters were Dynamic: `haxe_box_int_ptr` at every `new TreeNode`\nand `haxe_unbox_int_ptr` in the constructor — one heap box per node.\n\nTell in the MIR (`RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1`): `TreeNode.new($0: *void, $1: *void,\n$2: *void, $3: *void)` with `call @haxe_unbox_int_ptr($3)`; after the fix\n`$3: i32`. `RAYZOR_PARAM_INFER_LOG=1` printed nothing for `new`.\n\nFix: lower a class's non-function fields first, then run the inference,\nthen lower the functions. Methods are already pre-registered before either\npass, so field initialisers still resolve them; fields keep their source\norder among themselves.\n\nSeen on the way: the user's `TreeNode` lowers as `haxe.ds.TreeNode` (the\nBalancedTree node's symbol) — the same root-symbol sharing as 0b91874,\nharmless here but the qualified name is wrong.","files":null}]}